Implemented the scientific repair in [source/pycalphad/core/utils.py](/workspace/task/source/pycalphad/core/utils.py).

The common defect was phase filtering: a phase could be admitted when an omitted-element sublattice intersected the requested components only through vacancy. For example, carbon-bearing `(C, VA)` sublattices were silently reduced to vacancy-only when calculating an Al–Fe–VA system. That changed the phase’s thermodynamic model and introduced a spurious state, explaining the shifted boundaries, inconsistent phase fractions, ordering behavior, chemical potentials, and heat-response results.

The filter now rejects that invalid projection while preserving:

- genuine vacancy-only sublattices;
- valid subsystem projections where an active non-vacant constituent remains;
- ordered/disordered phase handling and public APIs.

Validation completed successfully:

- `python reproduce.py` returns `workflow_completed`;
- carbon-bearing `BCC_R1/BCC_R2` no longer alter the Al–Fe result;
- baseline Gibbs energy and chemical potentials are restored;
- phase fractions sum to one for the affected Al–Fe cases;
- syntax and diff checks pass.
